sd7|v|To set in order; to arrange, or lay away, esp. as papers in a methodical manner for preservation and reverence; to place on file; to insert in its proper place in an arranged body of papers. ; To bring before a court or legislative body by presenting proper papers in a regular way; as, to file a petition or bill. ; To put upon the files or among the records of a court; to note on (a paper) the fact date of its reception in court. ; To march in a file or line, as soldiers, not abreast, but one after another; -- generally with off. ; To rub, smooth, or cut away, with a file; to sharpen with a file; as, to file a saw or a tooth. ; To smooth or polish as with a file. ; To make foul; to defile.	s:1zoh,18,10;1k9x,14,4~1zoh,18,10;1k9x,14,4	D:5wq,1,3~5wq,1,3
