sg2|a|Finished; brought to perfection; refined; hence, free from impurity; excellent; superior; elegant; worthy of admiration; accomplished; beautiful. ; Aiming at show or effect; loaded with ornament; overdressed or overdecorated; showy. ; Nice; delicate; subtle; exquisite; artful; skillful; dexterous. ; Not coarse, gross, or heavy ; Not gross; subtile; thin; tenous. ; Not coarse; comminuted; in small particles; as, fine sand or flour. ; Not thick or heavy; slender; filmy; as, a fine thread. ; Thin; attenuate; keen; as, a fine edge. ; Made of fine materials; light; delicate; as, fine linen or silk. ; Having (such) a proportion of pure metal in its composition; as, coins nine tenths fine. ; (Used ironically.) ; To make fine; to refine; to purify, to clarify; as, to fine gold. ; To make finer, or less coarse, as in bulk, texture, etc.; as. to fine the soil. ; To change by fine gradations; as (Naut.), to fine down a ship's lines, to diminish her lines gradually.	j:1teg,70,9;1huh,68,3;wml,67,6;1hu4,59,11;262i,50,14;jwv,48,26;15t,48,6;1lzw,40,5;4vm,37,4;jwz,35,19;261x,35,4;n5q,27,2;176t,22,19;fq4,19,8;16eq,19,13~jwv,48,26;jwz,35,19;176t,22,19;262i,50,14;16eq,19,13;1hu4,59,11;1teg,70,9;fq4,19,8;wml,67,6;15t,48,6;1lzw,40,5;177e,11,5;261x,35,4;4vm,37,4;21fw,2,4	e:1ish,68,154;24ne,47,20;14yr,35,278;r9x,32,10;ba,30,7;1c3a,26,9;ekj,25,13;2911,18,59;1mzo,2,9;1p1y,1,5~14yr,35,278;1ish,68,154;2911,18,59;24ne,47,20;ekj,25,13;r9x,32,10;1mzo,2,9;1c3a,26,9;ba,30,7;1p1y,1,5
