sh5|n|That which finishes, puts an end to/ or perfects. ; The joiner work and other finer work required for the completion of a building, especially of the interior. See Inside finish, and Outside finish. ; The labor required to give final completion to any work; hence, minute detail, careful elaboration, or the like. ; See Finishing coat, under Finishing. ; The result of completed labor, as on the surface of an object; manner or style of finishing; as, a rough, dead, or glossy finish given to cloth, stone, metal, etc. ; Completion; -- opposed to start, or beginning.	a:1x71,64,3;1x6x,63,18;21fw,47,24~21fw,47,24;1x6x,63,18;1x71,64,3	n:19e0,82,5;21fw,54,40;1x71,48,1~21fw,54,40;19e0,82,5;1x71,48,1
